            "_type": "chapter",
            "_key": "ch1",
            "title": "A view counter nobody could measure",
            "text": [
              {
                "_type": "block",
                "_key": "ch1t0",
                "style": "normal",
                "markDefs": [],
                "children": [
                  {
                    "_type": "span",
                    "_key": "ch1t0s",
                    "text": "A Swedish fashion brand on a shared headless storefront asked for one thing in September: a product-page urgency element, a view counter. Lab mobile scores sat in the 30s, which became a second track.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "caption": "The product list in September. Zero products carried the bestseller badge because of a data bug.",
            "layout": "half",
            "side": "right",
            "media": {
              "type": "video",
              "video": {
                "_type": "file",
                "asset": {
                  "_type": "reference",
                  "_ref": "file-5d8a0223c690269db59bcbae2f9c1f21cd5f8c76-mp4"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "_type": "chapter",
            "_key": "ch2",
            "title": "Every test had been off since 1 July",
            "text": [
              {
                "_type": "block",
                "_key": "ch2t0",
                "style": "normal",
                "markDefs": [],
                "children": [
                  {
                    "_type": "span",
                    "_key": "ch2t0s",
                    "text": "A view counter is a number on a page. Nobody had asked whether a number would move anything, or whether the site could tell. The audit answered the second question first: a consent listener registered with once:true meant a user who declined cookies and then accepted never fired an exposure event.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "caption": "The product page on a phone, where the view counter was meant to go. Nine earlier tests had run on a broken instrument.",
            "layout": "wide",
            "side": "left",
            "media": {
              "type": "video",
              "video": {
                "_type": "file",
                "asset": {
                  "_type": "reference",
                  "_ref": "file-cda04703fbe80afe20474fc85bdeaa7f0a060ba6-mp4"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "_type": "chapter",
            "_key": "ch3",
            "title": "Five tests, one priority ladder",
            "text": [
              {
                "_type": "block",
                "_key": "ch3t0",
                "style": "normal",
                "markDefs": [],
                "children": [
                  {
                    "_type": "span",
                    "_key": "ch3t0s",
                    "text": "I reframed the ask from one widget to a programme: a research brief, two product-page audits, a decisions log and five candidate tests. A priority ladder decides which one a product shows, so two numbers never compete on one page.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "_type": "block",
                "_key": "ch3t1",
                "style": "normal",
                "markDefs": [],
                "children": [
                  {
                    "_type": "span",
                    "_key": "ch3t1s",
                    "text": "Each test was specced in Figma and prototyped in a product-page lab where stakeholders could flip arms before anything was coded. The client picked the bestseller badge and the countdown.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "caption": "The bestseller badge on the product list, the first of the five to ship. Control and variant from production, same session.",
            "layout": "full",
            "side": "right",
            "media": {
              "type": "video",
              "video": {
                "_type": "file",
                "asset": {
                  "_type": "reference",
                  "_ref": "file-1460e68fea5dd4d54cc2be90fc556b0c6b487cec-mp4"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "_type": "chapter",
            "_key": "ch4",
            "title": "Lighthouse 34 to 87, and 31 badged products",
            "text": [
              {
                "_type": "block",
                "_key": "ch4t0",
                "style": "normal",
                "markDefs": [],
                "children": [
                  {
                    "_type": "span",
                    "_key": "ch4t0s",
                    "text": "The bestseller badge shipped on 20 October as the first live test; badged products went from 0 to 31. The performance rebuild raised Lighthouse mobile from 34, 35 and 33 to 87, 83 and 82 on home, listing and product pages, with 133 of 151 parity checks passing and 0 failing.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
